cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these assets in research or published work, please cite this repository."
title: saddle-examples-Blender
type: software
version: 1.0.0-rc.1
date-released: "2026-04-30"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: https://github.com/EagleHorseTech/saddle-examples-Blender
abstract: >
  A collection of five western saddle tree STL meshes paired with Blender 5.1
  Python scripts that import each mesh, run a cleanup pass, and create
  named colour-coded boolean-tool primitives pre-positioned over anatomically
  correct saddle regions for Quarter Horse fitting.  Converted from the
  companion FreeCAD package (saddle-examples-FreeCAD).
keywords:
  - saddle
  - saddle tree
  - western saddle
  - blender
  - boolean modelling
  - horse fitting
  - equine
  - 3D modelling
